  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-ssh",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-ssh\" alt=\"npm version\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/l/dsh-ssh\" alt=\"license\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/node-%3E%3D22-339933\" alt=\"node version\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/UynajGI/dsh-ssh\" alt=\"GitHub stars\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-ssh",
      "text": "**SSH remote-execution plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness).** Runs Bash, file tools, PTY terminals and LSP on a remote host over one SSH connection — ProxyJump chains, SFTP, full auth. Built on [ssh2](https://github.com/mscdex/ssh2)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-ssh\n```\n\nOr use the Web UI: **Plugins → Add plugin → `dsh-ssh`**. The bundle mounts the SSH providers and takes over the **Add workspace** flow — create real connections there. Needs DeepSeek Harness 0.2.x and Node ≥ 22.\n\nA plain `npm i dsh-ssh` does not select the bundle; add it to `dsh.profile.bundles` yourself."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure",
      "text": "Only needed when composing providers by hand (`cordis.yml`):\n\n```yaml\n- id: ssh-remote\n  name: dsh-ssh\n  config:\n    host: server.example.com        # or a ~/.ssh/config alias"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure",
      "text": "| Field | Default | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `host` `username` `cwd` | — | required (`cwd` is an absolute POSIX path) |\n| `port` | 22 | |\n| `password` `privateKey` `passphrase` `agent` | — | any auth mode; falls back to `~/.ssh` identities |\n| `jump` | `[]` | ProxyJump chain, independent auth per hop |\n| `readyTimeout` `keepaliveInterval` `keepaliveCountMax` | 45000 / 0 / 3 | milliseconds |\n| `strictHostKeyChecking` `knownHosts` | false / `[]` | host-key verification |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configure",
      "text": "> **Web profile:** `subprocess` and `fs` are single-slot services. Disable the local providers (`dsh-subprocess-local`, `dsh-fs-sandbox`) in the profile patch, or remote work silently runs on the harness host."
    },
    {
      "section": "Limitations",
      "text": "- Remote pid is always `-1`; `terminate` doesn't reap descendants (SSH can't).\n- The SSH link doesn't auto-reconnect after a drop — recreate the connection.\n- `streamText` is text-only; remote sessions aren't added to the local workspace registry."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm i\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run build   # emits lib/ — the payload the harness loader imports\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
